{"concept":"counterfactual","groups":[{"id":"narrative-past","name":{"ru":"Повествовательное es war и направление назад","en":"Narrative es war and backward direction"},"count":21},{"id":"past-will","name":{"ru":"Совершившееся и желание назад","en":"The past and willing backwards"},"count":7}],"occurrences":[{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.01","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-fec3c8ac52ba7999af2cdf7b1a7d394d","tos.text-unit.sid-fec3c8ac52ba7999af2cdf7b1a7d394d"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["becoming","dance","rope-bridge"],"line":{"ru":"Ожидание канатного плясуна собирает народ для первой речи.","en":"Expectation of the tightrope walker gathers the people for the first speech."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-2853316493ea5378e18e6ba71f8c23b5","tos.text-unit.sid-2853316493ea5378e18e6ba71f8c23b5"]},"form":"Rückwärts","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["difference","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Люди смотрят назад, во времена, когда сомнение было грехом.","en":"The backward gaze seeks an age of belief and forbidden doubt."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-c515e160e9084b0952538c15223fc388","tos.text-unit.sid-c515e160e9084b0952538c15223fc388"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["spirit-of-gravity","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Торжественная серьёзность открывает дух тяжести.","en":"Solemn seriousness reveals the spirit of gravity."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-21fcc49e6c8df41fffd3f2cf04cbcfe3","tos.text-unit.sid-21fcc49e6c8df41fffd3f2cf04cbcfe3"]},"form":"rückwärts","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["will","identity","rope-bridge","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Тянущие нити уподоблены людям, которые сучат верёвку и пятятся.","en":"Those who spin rope pull their threads and walk backward."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-ae3e044dc13010d26eced91d029c9e51","tos.text-unit.sid-ae3e044dc13010d26eced91d029c9e51"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Прежнее убежище веры изображено спящим чудовищем.","en":"Faith’s former refuge is pictured as a sleeping monster."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-a75e78d3a1f43a3674ab4551a0c7233c","tos.text-unit.sid-a75e78d3a1f43a3674ab4551a0c7233c"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["agency","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Жрецы назвали Богом то, что противоречило им и причиняло боль.","en":"The priests called God what contradicted and hurt them."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9bcffed08072c8b5bc0beed4636e30ac","tos.text-unit.sid-9bcffed08072c8b5bc0beed4636e30ac"]},"form":"rückwärts","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Бегство назад приводит к современному миру культуры.","en":"Flight backwards leads to the contemporary world of culture."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5d7585f48e3c3ff7eef88bb204463cc3","tos.text-unit.sid-5d7585f48e3c3ff7eef88bb204463cc3"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["fate","will","creation","redemption","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Избавление превращает «было» в «так хотел я».","en":"Redemption transforms “it was” into “thus I willed it.”"}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-dc0a4af060b9be065759832a96bf8a51","tos.text-unit.sid-dc0a4af060b9be065759832a96bf8a51"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["will","agency","loneliness","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"«Было» — сокровенное горе воли, бессильной изменить прошлое.","en":"“It was” is the will’s secret sorrow, powerless to change the past."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-d0da4f88d01d03d4f85805f9f62a77be","tos.text-unit.sid-d0da4f88d01d03d4f85805f9f62a77be"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["will","affirmation","identity","revenge","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мщение названо отвращением воли ко времени и к его «было».","en":"Revenge is named the will’s aversion to time and its “It was.”"}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-53738e68984ce6b12c1e7d49b70cd7ba","tos.text-unit.sid-53738e68984ce6b12c1e7d49b70cd7ba"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["redemption","zarathustra","revenge-madness"],"line":{"ru":"«Безумие» выводит вечное наказание из несдвигаемого прошлого.","en":"“Madness” derives eternal punishment from the immovable past."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-cad70ec5a95e4aa4ebec565f3f3a9d3b","tos.text-unit.sid-cad70ec5a95e4aa4ebec565f3f3a9d3b"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["fate","will","creation","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Созидающая воля отвечает прошлому: «Но так хотела я!»","en":"Creative will answers the past with its own willing."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-351ef082d5a4c98dcd346a2cbfc1357f","tos.text-unit.sid-351ef082d5a4c98dcd346a2cbfc1357f"]},"form":"Zurückwollen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["will-to-power","will","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Воля к власти достигает вопроса о желании назад.","en":"Will to power reaches the question of willing backwards."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-4979fb4ab5e7de21fc9d81049b413a86","tos.text-unit.sid-4979fb4ab5e7de21fc9d81049b413a86"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["will","becoming","identity","agency","attention"],"line":{"ru":"Выслушивание моряков освобождает собственную речь учителя.","en":"Listening to sailors frees the teacher’s own speech."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-dff926efa83f3da3ee1d67d9a3e0538b","tos.text-unit.sid-dff926efa83f3da3ee1d67d9a3e0538b"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["gateway","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Появление ворот следует за освобождением плеч от карлика.","en":"The gateway appears after the shoulders are freed from the dwarf."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-b8cef20c095784beb2dd363f1a0e98cb","tos.text-unit.sid-b8cef20c095784beb2dd363f1a0e98cb"]},"form":"rückwärts","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["present","gateway","two-paths","eternity","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"От этого мгновения дорога уходит назад в вечность.","en":"From this moment the path stretches backwards into eternity."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.03","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-b09619382c528645115f3ad6bde0f1a8","tos.text-unit.sid-b09619382c528645115f3ad6bde0f1a8"]},"form":"rückwärts","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Неопределённое море заставляет смотреть вперёд и назад.","en":"The uncertain sea makes one look forwards and backwards."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-c1cdda843f95bcd960ce245cf3a90257","tos.text-unit.sid-c1cdda843f95bcd960ce245cf3a90257"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"past-will","neighbours":["fate","will","becoming","creation","redemption","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Прошлое должно быть спасено и преобразовано, пока воля не скажет: «Так хотела я! Так захочу я!»","en":"The past is to receive the will’s own desire."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.05","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-e4773abbfcbda81dd8e326c351fb37cf","tos.text-unit.sid-e4773abbfcbda81dd8e326c351fb37cf"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["will","identity","necessity","circle","earth"],"line":{"ru":"Крик помощи приводит учителя к играющему страдание чародею.","en":"The cry for help brings the teacher to a magician performing suffering."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.05","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-584ffd54dd7e1b17ba4cc75b3f575ece","tos.text-unit.sid-584ffd54dd7e1b17ba4cc75b3f575ece"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"magician","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["innocence-play","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Игра чародея обнаруживает долю подлинного покаяния.","en":"The magician’s performance reveals a share of genuine penitence."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-ae7203a509b556a108734563b353cc54","tos.text-unit.sid-ae7203a509b556a108734563b353cc54"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"last-pope","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["difference","last-pope"],"line":{"ru":"Скрытность Бога изображена обходным путём рождения сына.","en":"God’s secrecy is pictured through the circuitous begetting of a son."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6cb2bc71c2fccf8842ebe8e00d73046b","tos.text-unit.sid-6cb2bc71c2fccf8842ebe8e00d73046b"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"last-pope","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["affirmation","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель ценит ясность взгляда и прямоту речи.","en":"The teacher values a clear gaze and honest speech."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.07","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-23cea31ffebada3de8540709c2e0d28a","tos.text-unit.sid-23cea31ffebada3de8540709c2e0d28a"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["becoming"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра входит в долину Смерти змей, царство смерти среди скал.","en":"The valley of snakes’ deaths introduces a realm of dead landscape."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.10","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-503af5c75da34d0215d3d724ba5d5809","tos.text-unit.sid-503af5c75da34d0215d3d724ba5d5809"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra-soul","mode":"dream","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра считает хулой свои прежние слова о том, как мало нужно для счастья.","en":"Zarathustra calls his former words about how little happiness needs blasphemy."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-cbca3c4a61fb282f2239ab51b47f8f88","tos.text-unit.sid-cbca3c4a61fb282f2239ab51b47f8f88"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["great-noon","identity","necessity","difference","attention"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра слышит в своей пещере крик, состоящий из многих голосов.","en":"Zarathustra hears a cry made up of many voices in his cave."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-14a37ae01737e3188609ec1ebbf8b184","tos.text-unit.sid-14a37ae01737e3188609ec1ebbf8b184"]},"form":"Es war","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"magician","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["agency","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель спрашивает чародея о его участии в нелепом поклонении.","en":"The teacher asks the magician about his part in absurd worship."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9c2be175d324e0a3bebdd65d440d241e","tos.text-unit.sid-9c2be175d324e0a3bebdd65d440d241e"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"magician","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["becoming","magician"],"line":{"ru":"Чародей признаёт тяжесть собственной глупости.","en":"The magician admits the weight of his folly."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.19","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-506672d69d74c231eab0ee3056459a6a","tos.text-unit.sid-506672d69d74c231eab0ee3056459a6a"]},"form":"es war","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"narrative-past","neighbours":["becoming","identity","difference","attention","laughter","dance"],"line":{"ru":"Услышанный вопрос открывает гостям собственное выздоровление.","en":"The heard question reveals their own recovery to the guests."}}]}
